'''''Lampranthus falciformis''''', commonly known as the '''sickle-leaved dewplant''',  is a succulent plant belonging to the genus ''[[Lampranthus]]''.<ref>{{Cite web|title=Lampranthus falciformis (Haw.) N.E.Br.|url=http://redlist.sanbi.org/species.php?species=88-79|work=SANBI Redlist}}</ref> The species is endemic to the [[Western Cape]]. Population numbers are stable.<ref>{{Cite web|title=Lampranthus falciformis (Haw.) N.E.Br.|url=https://powo.science.kew.org/taxon/urn:lsid:ipni.org:names:362217-1|work=Plants of the World Online}}</ref>

